{"name":"Avalon","hex":"#799b96","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Avalon","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An island, represented as an earthly paradise in the western seas, to which King Arthur and other heroes were carried at death.","A city in Santa Catalina Island, Los Angeles County, California, United States, North America."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Avalon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Avalon","blocks":[{"text":"Avalon is an island featured in the Arthurian legend. It first appeared in Geoffrey of Monmouth's 1136 Historia Regum Britanniae as a place of magic where King Arthur's sword Excalibur was made and later where Arthur was taken to recover from being gravely wounded at the Battle of Camlann. Since then, the island has become a symbol of Arthurian mythology, similar to Arthur's castle, Camelot."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Burne-Jones_Last_Sleep_of_Arthur_in_Avalon_v2.jpg/330px-Burne-Jones_Last_Sleep_of_Arthur_in_Avalon_v2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Avalon"},{"title":"Avalon (American group)","blocks":[{"text":"Avalon, also known as Avalon Worship, is an American contemporary Christian vocal quartet from Nashville and was formed in 1995. The group has earned multiple RIAA-certified gold records. The group consists of Janna Long, Greg Long, and Jody McBrayer. The newest fourth member has yet to be revealed."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Avalon_(American_group)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/The_Death_of_King_Arthur.jpg/500px-The_Death_of_King_Arthur.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/The_Death_of_King_Arthur.jpg/500px-The_Death_of_King_Arthur.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thum